# Owner-sensitive strategic context — local-only by design, never commit.
# Carries personal/venture information that must not enter this public repo.
# If absent after a fresh clone, the canonical copy lives in the owner's ace-wiki.
docs/VENTURE-CONTEXT.md

# Traffic snapshots. Public repo: publishing traffic figures is a business
# decision, not a side effect of running a script.
analytics/

# Audit working files. Public repo: findings get triaged into commits and docs,
# not dumped wholesale.
audit-defects.json
audit-plan.md

# CaribStat harvested data. THE HARD RULE FOR THIS DIRECTORY.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC (verified: gh repo view asokore/statcite -> PUBLIC).
# caribstat/data/ holds ~28MB of ECCB and Central Bank of Barbados series.
#
# The reason for this rule CHANGED on 2026-08-14 and the note is corrected to
# match. It used to be a licence rule: the ledger recorded both sources as "not
# served ... its website terms do not permit the redistribution this service
# would perform". The operator has since obtained written permission from both
# banks and those ledger entries now read "served" (verified against the live
# ledger at https://statcite.com/v1/sources on 2026-08-15).
#
# It is now a canonical-location rule, and it is just as firm. The collected
# JSON is published at github.com/asokore/caribstat, which is the location the
# ledger's `access` field names and the Worker fetches. Committing the same
# files here would create a second copy that can silently drift from the one
# actually being served. Never `git add caribstat/data`, never force it with
# -f. Whether that ever changes is the operator's decision, not an agent's.
caribstat/data/
caribstat/*.log
caribstat/node_modules/

# Raw source workbooks and scraped reference artefacts kept for debugging the
# parsers. Same licence status as the harvested data: these ARE the banks'
# published files, so they never go to the public remote either.
caribstat/reference/

# tools/publish-run.mjs's staging clone. This is a working copy of a
# DIFFERENT public repository (github.com/asokore/caribstat), used only to
# sync the local harvest there. It has its own .git and its own remote and
# must never be mistaken for part of this repository.
caribstat/.publish/
